>> title: All-Butter Pie Crust
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: pastry, pie, butter, dough, make-ahead
>> counters: Bakery, Diner, Meat and Three
>> aka: pie dough, pie shell, double crust, shortcrust, pâte brisée, pate brisee
>> pairs-with: french-vanilla-ice-cream
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 20 min

>> step: whisk the dry mix
Whisk @all-purpose flour{2 1/2%cup}(315 g), @granulated sugar{1%Tbs}(12 g), and @fine sea salt{1%tsp}(6 g) together.

>> step: rub in the butter to pea-size pieces
Rub @cold unsalted butter{1%cup}(226 g; cut in 1/2-in cubes) into @&(~1)dry mix{} until the biggest pieces are the size of peas.

>> step: sprinkle in, toss to a shaggy dough
Sprinkle @ice water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and @cider vinegar{1%tsp}(5 mL) over @&(~1)buttered flour{} and toss to a shaggy dough.

>> step: press into two discs, chill 1 hour
Press @&(~1)shaggy dough{} into two discs, wrap, and ~chill{60%min}.

>> step: roll into two 12-in rounds
Roll @&(~1)chilled discs{} out on a board dusted with @flour for the board{2%Tbs}(16 g) into two 12-in rounds.
